<p>North Korea fired multiple ballistic missiles toward the sea off its east coast on Sunday. South Korea said the launches came from the Sinpo area, while Japan said the missiles appeared to have fallen near the Korean Peninsula’s east coast. South Korea’s military called them short-range ballistic missiles, and Japanese authorities said they had not confirmed any incursion into Japan’s exclusive economic zone. The launch was the seventh reported ballistic missile test this year and the fourth in April, continuing Pyongyang’s rapid pace of weapons activity. South Korea’s presidential office called an emergency security meeting and described the launches as a provocation that violated U.N. Security Council resolutions. Analysts cited in the coverage said the tests appear linked to North Korea’s broader push to strengthen its military and nuclear capabilities.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/7whW8R2hhod0iqVgK-IWj3O3DlR9WZiopqqfRUPKdY8xYIb-AbSOrUcBNrDb3nia5V3QIlhSUk2yYGUhCD8wU11VHPI2MUDpygKzZ3am05WU' alt='North Korean leader Kim Jong Un speaks during a Workers’ Party meeting in Pyongyang on February 23, 2026.' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Flight distance: South Korea said the missiles flew about 140 kilometers before landing in the sea.</li><li>Leverage motive: Experts cited by Dawn said Pyongyang’s intense missile activity appears aimed at showcasing self-defence capabilities while building international leverage.</li><li>Dialogue backdrop: The launches came as President Trump, preparing for a summit in China next month, and South Korean President Lee Jae Myung both signaled interest in talks with Kim Jong Un, though no meeting plans are publicly known.</li></ul><blockquote>As the U.S. is focused on Iran, the North sees this as a golden time to upgrade their nuclear power and missile capability, - Lim Eul-chul</blockquote><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>South Korea&#x27;s presidential office: It called an emergency security meeting and described the launches as a provocation that violated U.N. Security Council resolutions. (<a href='https://www.dawn.com/news/1993180/north-korea-fires-ballistic-missiles-again-flexing-muscle-amid-iran-war'>Dawn</a>)</li><li>Japanese government: It said the missiles were believed to have fallen near the Korean Peninsula’s east coast and that authorities had not confirmed any entry into Japan’s exclusive economic zone. (<a href='https://www.dawn.com/news/1993180/north-korea-fires-ballistic-missiles-again-flexing-muscle-amid-iran-war'>Dawn</a>)</li><li>Analysts cited by Euronews: They said the short-range missile tests signal that Pyongyang is rejecting South Korea’s recent attempts to ease tensions. (<a href='http://www.euronews.com/2026/04/19/north-korea-conducts-multiple-ballistic-missile-tests'>Euronews</a>)</li><li>Kim Ki-jung, former South Korean security adviser: He said the launches appear intended to increase pressure ahead of any dialogue with the United States and South Korea. (<a href='https://www.dawn.com/news/1993180/north-korea-fires-ballistic-missiles-again-flexing-muscle-amid-iran-war'>Dawn</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://www.al-monitor.com/originals/2026/04/north-korea-fires-multiple-ballistic-missiles-towards-sea-its-east-coast'>North Korea fires multiple ballistic missiles towards sea off its east coast</a> - al-monitor.com</li><li><a href='http://www.euronews.com/2026/04/19/north-korea-conducts-multiple-ballistic-missile-tests'>North Korea conducts multiple ballistic missile tests</a> - euronews.com</li><li><a href='https://www.dawn.com/news/1993180/north-korea-fires-ballistic-missiles-again-flexing-muscle-amid-iran-war'>North Korea fires ballistic missiles again, flexing muscle amid Iran war</a> - dawn.com</li><li><a href='https://www.aljazeera.com/news/2026/4/19/north-korea-launches-ballistic-missiles-towards-sea-off-its-east-coast'>North Korea launches ballistic missiles towards sea off its east coast</a> - aljazeera.com</li><li><a href='ht